  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 104,
  "title": "Psalms 104",
  "display_title": "Psalms 104",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 104,
  "sortOrder": 19104,
  "verseCount": 35,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honour and majesty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Who coverest thyself with light as with a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Who laid the foundations of the earth, that it should not be removed for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Thou coveredst it with the deep as with a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys unto the place which thou hast founded for them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "He sendeth the springs into the valleys, which run among the hills.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, which sing among the branches.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And wine that maketh glad the heart of man, and oil to make his face to shine, and bread which strengtheneth man’s heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The trees of the LORD are full of sap; the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Where the birds make their nests: as for the stork, the fir trees are her house.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "The high hills are a refuge for the wild goats; and the rocks for the conies.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "He appointed the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Thou makest darkness, and it is night: wherein all the beasts of the forest do creep forth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their meat from God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "The sun ariseth, they gather themselves together, and lay them down in their dens.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Man goeth forth unto his work and to his labour until the evening.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "So is this great and wide sea, wherein are things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "There go the ships: there is that leviathan, whom thou hast made to play therein.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give them their meat in due season.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "That thou givest them they gather: thou openest thine hand, they are filled with good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "The glory of the LORD shall endure for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in his works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "I will sing unto the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:104:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "Let the sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 104:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:104:35"
      }
    }
  ],
